  <sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
    <selectionEntryGroup id="c96f-43cd-af76-7458" name="Ork Vehicle Upgrades" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true">
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry id="6a5c-da38-6643-b8d7" name="Armor Plates" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="55b1-a746-9665-c327" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="d7df-9a64-35f3-57c6" name="Armor Plates" hidden="false">
              <description>Roll a D6 for each glancing or penetrating hit caused against the vehicle. On a 6 the hit is ignored. </description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="5.0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="9a63-4284-5b32-ab43" name="Big Grabber" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="d017-a881-5b2c-66be" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="59ff-672e-0c20-b50d" name="Big Grabber" hidden="false">
              <description>An Ork vehicle with a Big Grabba make attack an enemy vehicle in close combat. The Ork vehicle must move into contact with the target vehicle during its movement phase but may not attack if it moved more than 12&quot;.
The Ork vehicle may shoot in the shooting phase as normal and then resolves an attack in the assault phase. The vehicle has one attack for each upgrade listed (Big Grabber/Wrecker Ball/Reinforced Ram/Boarding Plank). Attacks hit on a 4+ regardless of the target&apos;s speed and are resolved with a Strength of 6. Walkers, skimmers, infantry and any other models that have a WS characteristic may not be attacked by these weapons.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="5.0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="f4d6-0e9a-4be3-d234" name="Boarding Plank" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="e894-e778-bb5e-b2e4" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="40c4-5956-d3f7-d01b" name="Boarding Plank" hidden="false">
              <description>An Ork vehicle with a Big Grabba make attack an enemy vehicle in close combat. The Ork vehicle must move into contact with the target vehicle during its movement phase but may not attack if it moved more than 12&quot;.
The Ork vehicle may shoot in the shooting phase as normal and then resolves an attack in the assault phase. The vehicle has one attack for each upgrade listed (Big Grabber/Wrecker Ball/Reinforced Ram/Boarding Plank). Attacks hit on a 4+ regardless of the target&apos;s speed and are resolved with a Strength of 6. Walkers, skimmers, infantry and any other models that have a WS characteristic may not be attacked by these weapons.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="5.0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="4055-2a61-cde6-2d0d" name="Grot Riggers" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="dab9-ee8c-6de9-ea64" type="max"/>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="5fbf-adca-a0f8-6b0b" type="min"/>
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="ed2f-ba57-a4c2-5b02" name="Grot Riggers" hidden="false">
              <description>An immobilised Ork vehicle with Grot Riggers on board may make a test at the start of each Ork turn. Roll a D6, on a result of 4+ the immobilised status is removed.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="2.0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="69bb-10c3-672e-1a1c" name="Bolt-on Big Shoota" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="e5d1-6011-44b8-d12f" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="f14d-f888-9148-22af" name="Bolt-on Big Shoota" hidden="false">
              <description>A bolt-on big shoota can only be mounted on a wartrukk. It can be fired by one of da boyz onboard who is a passanger as long as the wartrukk itself does not move more than 12&quot; that turn.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="10.0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="4668-98f7-8757-2dfc" name="Red Paint Job" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="b3b2-231e-b215-d8f8" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="5d8d-2e5a-773d-c469" name="Red Paint Job" hidden="false">
              <description>An Ork vehicle with a red paint job adds +1&quot; to all of its move distances. For example, a fast Ork vehicle with a red paint job could move 13&quot; and still fire one weapon and/or disembark troops, or move 25&quot; and not fire at all.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="3.0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="c504-c288-9032-5709" name="Reinforced Ram" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="d2f2-0993-7eb3-2f81" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="dcb6-cbf9-037e-790c" name="Reinforced Ram" hidden="false">
              <description>An Ork vehicle with a Big Grabba make attack an enemy vehicle in close combat. The Ork vehicle must move into contact with the target vehicle during its movement phase but may not attack if it moved more than 12&quot;.
The Ork vehicle may shoot in the shooting phase as normal and then resolves an attack in the assault phase. The vehicle has one attack for each upgrade listed (Big Grabber/Wrecker Ball/Reinforced Ram/Boarding Plank). Attacks hit on a 4+ regardless of the target&apos;s speed and are resolved with a Strength of 6. Walkers, skimmers, infantry and any other models that have a WS characteristic may not be attacked by these weapons.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="5.0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="f021-2830-73a4-df4f" name="Searchlight" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="0093-3e88-4f6d-a688" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="f409-df08-7acd-1393" name="Searchlight" hidden="false">
              <description>Searchlights are only used in missions where the rules for night fighting are being used. They allow one enemy unit spotted by the vehicle or Dreadnought to be fired at by all other Ork units that are in range and have a line of fire. However, the vehicle or Dreadnought using the Searchlight in this manner is considered visible to all enemy units who have line of sight on the next turn.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="1.0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="460c-853e-e6ad-4dc3" name="Spikes &apos;n Blades" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="8cb5-bb29-cb19-1995" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="c2f0-0094-e7b9-b8b9" name="Spikes &apos;n Blades" hidden="false">
              <description>Enemy infantry which try to attack a vehicle that has spikes &apos;n blades in close combat and miss suffer a S3 hit. </description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="5.0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="c7fe-7bd3-b18c-487f" name="Stikkabomb Chucka" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="0ff1-73a3-2d52-ad35" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="6928-14ed-3534-6616" name="Stikkabomb Chucka" hidden="false">
              <description>A vehicle or Dreadnought equipped with stikkbomb chuckas can make a Tank Shock attack even though it isn&apos;t a tank. A vehicle may not move more than 12&quot; and attempt to tank shock and a Dradnought can only attempt a Tank Shock attack in its movement phase. In the assault phase it must move into close combat instead. If a proper tank is equipped with stikkbomb chuckas any tank shock it inflicts has an extra -1 modifier to the troop&apos;s Morale check.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="3.0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="f085-89b0-80ff-1c02" name="Turbo Boosta" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="96a1-65b1-61f1-d3c1" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="cd09-e8d0-5904-fd3e" name="Turbo Boosta" hidden="false">
              <description>A vehicle with turbo boostas can trigger them in any of its movement phases. The trubo boostas add D6&quot; to its movement, but for shooting and disembarking troops the vehicle counts as moving at the speed it went before the turbo boosters were added. The extra D&quot; movement must be used to move in a straight line and if a 4+ is rolled the vehicle and any passengers onboard may not shoot or disembark that turn as they are too busy hanging on for grim death.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="5.0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="4068-5375-9020-222c" name="Wrecker Ball" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="ad35-4ec1-8e71-5a4c" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="74c7-44c8-f672-700a" name="Wrecker Ball" hidden="false">
              <description>An Ork vehicle with a Big Grabba make attack an enemy vehicle in close combat. The Ork vehicle must move into contact with the target vehicle during its movement phase but may not attack if it moved more than 12&quot;.
The Ork vehicle may shoot in the shooting phase as normal and then resolves an attack in the assault phase. The vehicle has one attack for each upgrade listed (Big Grabber/Wrecker Ball/Reinforced Ram/Boarding Plank). Attacks hit on a 4+ regardless of the target&apos;s speed and are resolved with a Strength of 6. Walkers, skimmers, infantry and any other models that have a WS characteristic may not be attacked by these weapons.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="5.0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="4a3b-054e-a33b-6ff4" name="Armoured Top" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="1661-8d57-7272-46a9" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="a13a-93c0-838f-c592" name="Armoured Top" hidden="false"/>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="8.0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="0bdb-374c-bb92-7d70" name="Force Field" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="27c9-f33f-28b2-108a" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="0e78-bb0f-23b7-0b75" name="Force Field" hidden="false"/>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="5.0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
